      "sequence_position": 11,
      "problem": "If $[a]_{n}$ denotes the residue class containing all integers congruent to $a$ modulo $n,$ then $[-17]_{8}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We have $[a]_{8}=[b]_{8}$ if \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8).\n$$\n\nThe residue class $[-17]_{8}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $-17$ modulo $8.$ \n\nWe can find an alternative representation for this residue class as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[-17]_{8} & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡-17\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡(-3)\\cdot 8+7\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡(-3)\\cdot 0+7\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡7\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)} \\\\  & =[7]_{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
